<gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" creator="SWERefactorBench" version="1.1">
<metadata>
<name>fw07 map-matching fixture: Carretera General, Andorra</name>
<desc>Fourteen points along a 2366 m highway=primary way, taken from the node
coordinates of core/files/andorra.osm.gz itself and thinned to every seventh
point. Derived from the graph's own input rather than hand-typed so the trace is
guaranteed to lie on a road the car profile can traverse: an invented trace would
map-match to something on both sides and the differential would still pass, while
quietly grading the error path instead of the matcher. Timestamps are fixed at
8 s spacing from a constant instant, not generated, because this file is committed
and both sides must be asked about identical bytes.</desc>
<copyright author="OpenStreetMap contributors"/>
</metadata>
